uying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Monopar Therapeutics Inc., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, engages in developing therapeutics for the treatment of cancer in the United States. The company develops ALXN1840, a late-stage, investigational once-daily and oral medicine; MNPR-101, a proprietary humanized monoclonal antibody that is conjugated with different radioisotopes for the treatment of advanced solid tumors expressing urokinase plasminogen activator receptor; and MNPR-101-Zr, which is in phase 1 imaging and dosimetry clinical trial, a radiopharmaceutical imaging agent comprised of MNPR-101 conjugated to zirconium-89. It develops MNPR-101-Lu, a Phase1a stage radiotherapeutic comprised of MNPR-101 conjugated to actinium-225. The company has collaborations NorthStar to develop radio-immuno-therapeutics targeting severe COVID-19; Excel Diagnostics and Nuclear Oncology Center, for the investigational imaging agent MNPR-101-Zr and investigational therapeutic agent MNPR-101-Lu; license agreement with Alexion to develop and commercialize ALXN1840, a drug candidate for Wilson disease. The company was founded in 2014 and is headquartered in Wilmette, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Chandler D. Robinson M.B.A., M.D., M.Sc. | Co-Founder, CEO, President & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22 people. Stock-based compensation of $220K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Monopar Therapeutics Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $479M market cap on $0 of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -1004% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 23% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","St